# How to

These recipes assume you can already preview a component. Each page has one
goal. Exact syntax lives in [reference](/docs/reference/).

## Components and markup

- [Author components](/docs/how-to/author-components/) — declare, call, props, body, library layout
- [Write markup](/docs/how-to/write-markup/) — tags, fragments, attributes, interpolation
- [Use directives](/docs/how-to/use-directives/) — `@if`, `@for`, `@match`, `@let`

## Applications

- [Update the UI](/docs/how-to/update-the-ui/) — choose a fragment, command, or live stream
- [Handle requests and errors](/docs/how-to/handle-requests-and-errors/) — request access, `?`, logging, SQLite

## Workflow and tools

- [Develop and inspect](/docs/how-to/develop-and-inspect/) — run, view, browse, inspect, Dev panel
- [Use the playground](/docs/how-to/use-the-playground/) — WASM versus local mode
- [Set up editors](/docs/how-to/set-up-editors/) — VS Code and Zed

## Configuration and shipping

- [Configure and secure](/docs/how-to/configure-and-secure/) — `rocci.toml`, origins, Datastar pin
- [Package and deploy](/docs/how-to/package-and-deploy/) — release server, container, ad-hoc `.app`
